<BaseLayout title="COP Mobile privacy information — VCode" description="How COP Mobile handles location, reports, notifications and communication data." lang="en" path="/en/cop-mobile/privacy/" alternatePath="/cop-mobile/privacy/">
  <article class="guide"><a class="back-link" href="/en/app-store/cop-mobile/">← COP Mobile</a><header><p class="kicker">Privacy</p><h1>COP Mobile</h1><p>Information about data used to provide features selected by the user. Updated 22 September 2026.</p></header><div class="guide-body">
    <h2>Location and map</h2><p>Location access supports showing your position on the map, navigation and features you start. Sharing a location or report with COP is a separate visible action.</p>
    <h2>Reports, media and notifications</h2><p>A submitted report may include text, a selected location and media attached by the user. Notifications deliver selected alerts and communication events.</p>
    <h2>Communication</h2><p>Chat and calls use the signed-in account identity and technical data required to deliver and secure communication. The app does not expose internal credentials for map or server services.</p>
    <h2>Permissions and control</h2><p>You can change access to location, camera, microphone and notifications in iOS Settings at any time. Removing access may disable the related feature.</p>
    <h2>Contact</h2><p>Send privacy questions to <a href="mailto:podpora@zeleznalady.cz">podpora@zeleznalady.cz</a>. Never include passwords, tokens or your complete location history.</p>
  </div></article>
</BaseLayout>
